From 9fde88d68f6fefc6b73c58814eba612145baa2f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:57:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH HELD FOR HIS OK] Build 89 note 2: Theology's four pages
 revamped in the house style

Doctrine, Topics, Heresies and Apologetics, the pages behind Theology's
four buttons. His word of 2026-11-10: "it still looks like the old version,
and it still looks AI like vibe coded slop ... revamp it using our style".
The four buttons (TheologyLibrary.tsx) and the hub's page are not touched.
The plan and the record are docs/1.9-build/notes/theology-fable.md.

Each page wears its own bar (the way's name, back to Theology, the search
turned to Theology) and one shared frame, components/theology/WayPage.tsx:
the head is the button grown (the same lit glyph, name, kind and count),
then the page's one line; the body is the way's own form; the foot is the
page's note (the old lede, the same words) and the other three ways as the
hub's rows. The nameless back bar, the "Theology" label, the row of four
pills, the giant headline and the floating search pill are gone from these
four.

- Doctrine: shelves by subject in the order of the Creed, each under its
  subject's icon whole on a plate; its studies in one tray, each wearing
  the face of the Father it quotes most, with its length, its part or its
  check (StudyShelves.tsx, from the path's own studies).
- Topics: a card for each question in the order of the Creed, its
  subject's icon on a plate, its short answer and its citations. The
  German written into the page gives way to the catalog's keys.
- Heresies: the centuries in order, each a tray of its errors, the scroll
  on its plate, the name and the registry's one line.
- Apologetics: the objections by kind, each answer a card with its line
  and its summary whole.

A Father's face in its round frame is cut about his face, from the place
the app already records for each portrait (saintFaces.ts, faceShift):
St Basil's stood half out of it. Theology's faces only; Today's saint draws
as before.

No new words: every line is a key all 21 catalogs hold, or a registry's
own. lib/theology/__tests__/ways.test.ts holds the bars, the counts (the
hub's own), every study to a shelf, the grey shares every palette lifts,
no side stripe and no line cut short.

Checked on the export: mock-check passes on each of the four on all five
palettes and in Arabic's direction; words on raised trays, which it cannot
measure, are 4.99:1 or more on every palette; axe finds nothing on Dark or
Light.

